Modifications
-------------
  Modified by SkyTekx (Florian Kleber), 2026-11-02: backported from NeoForge 1.21.1 to Forge 1.20.1
  (Forge 47) for the SkyTekx 3 modpack, built against the SkyTekx fork of The Twilight Forest
  (4.3.2508-skytekx.1, which carries most Twilight Forest 4.8 content). The modified source is the
  ports/spiced-twilight directory of the skytekx3-1201-server repository; it is the Corresponding
  Source of the jar spiced_twilight-2.0.0-1.20.1-skytekx.1.jar. The mod id (spiced_twilight), item,
  entity and loot ids are unchanged.

  Removed
  - Naga jump attack (NagaMovementPatternMixin). Its mixin into the Naga movement pattern conflicts
    with Alternative Twilight Remastered, which is backported into the same pack and reworks the Naga.
    The Naga behaves as in Twilight Forest.

  Ported (same behavior, 1.20.1 APIs)
  - NeoForge data attachments -> synced entity data and entity NBT. The Helmet Crab hide flag is a
    synced entity data value; cooldown and hide chance are saved under "SpicedTwilightHide". The baby
    kobold flag is a synced entity data value, saved as "IsBaby" as upstream does.
  - LivingIncomingDamageEvent -> LivingAttackEvent, EntityTickEvent -> LivingTickEvent,
    RegisterSpawnPlacementsEvent -> SpawnPlacementRegisterEvent, DeferredHolder -> RegistryObject.
  - neoforge:add_table loot modifier -> spiced_twilight:add_table (Forge 47 has no built-in one), with
    forge:loot_table_id conditions and data/forge/loot_modifiers/global_loot_modifiers.json.
  - Cinder Pouch: the 1.21 bundle_contents component -> the 1.20.1 bundle NBT layout ("Items" list,
    capacity 64 Fire Beetle Powder). The 1.21 lore component -> a tooltip line in the lore style.
  - Loot tables: enchanted_count_increase -> looting_enchant, random_chance_with_enchanted_bonus ->
    random_chance_with_looting (same odds); 1.20.1 folder names (loot_tables/, recipes/,
    advancements/); the recipe and its advancement in the 1.20.1 datagen format.
  - EntityType.Builder#eyeHeight -> getEyeHeight override; baby kobolds use the 1.20.1 baby scale
    (half size) plus an eye height override.
  - All mixins re-targeted to the fork's classes and verified against its reobfuscated jar; a refmap
    is generated. The model setupAnim injections use remap = false because the typed overloads keep
    their names in the reobfuscated Twilight Forest jar.
  - LichAbsorbMinionsGoal: the injection sits at HEAD instead of right after super.tick() (Goal#tick
    is empty, so this is the same point). The "Lich is invisible after a teleport" check is looked up
    at runtime until the fork's Lich gains getTeleportInvisibility.
  - The kobold and helmet crab model mixins also apply to the fork's separate Jappa-pack model classes
    (NewKoboldModel, NewHelmetCrabModel); 4.8 keeps both layer definitions in one class.
  - The Maze Slime Beetle always renders with the default slime beetle model, which its texture is
    laid out for.

  Changed
  - Maze Slime Beetle spawning. Upstream's biome modifier adds it to #twilightforest:valid_labyrinth_biomes
    and names a structure tag, but NeoForge's add_spawns ignores the structure field, so upstream spawns
    it on the swamp surface. Twilight Forest replaces the spawn list inside its landmarks, so a biome
    modifier cannot reach the Labyrinth. The backport adds it (weight 3, group 1-2) through
    LevelEvent.PotentialSpawns to the monster spawns inside structures tagged
    #spiced_twilight:labyrinth_maze_slime_spawn (the Labyrinth, while it is not conquered).
  - Hiding Helmet Crabs still take damage that bypasses invulnerability (/kill, the void).

  Fixed upstream bugs
  - Kobold heads keep turning: upstream calls head.resetPose() after setupAnim, which also wiped the
    look rotation; only the head position is reset now.
  - Kobolds that roll Steeleaf Boots wear them on the feet (upstream put them into the head slot).
  - Helmet Crab hide state is saved (the upstream serializer returned null).
  - The horn tips stay visible while a Helmet Crab hides.
  - Maze Slime Ball splat particles are sent before the projectile is removed, and the Lich's shatter
    animation runs before the minion is converted, so clients receive both.
  - Dyed armor on kobolds renders the overlay layer untinted, as vanilla does.
